    {
      "id": "evidence-001-notes",
      "kind": {
        "text": "Enumerates the built Int environment over the FULL trusted surface (Axiom/Opaque/Quotient) and exits non-zero on any member. Environment-wide on purpose, and sound as a footprint bound for the same reason the Nat rows are: a theorem cannot depend on a trusted declaration the environment does not contain, so an empty surface bounds every individual footprint by []. Measured 2026-08-16: `ok: integer trusted surface = 0`, down from 34 when the construction began.",
